Again, think about addresses (e.g. 11A; technically is a number - do we 
have to use pa'ypa'y just because of the A at the end of it?), registration 
numbers, etc.

We can rework systems like my date system or Pierre's coordinate system to 
fit whatever Lojban evolves to, since they are meant for Lojbanic use. But 
we can't rework every irregular numeric system in everyday life.

